8045232</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-58046097-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>58046097</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5853764-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5853764</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1116743A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>JP NAT INST OF SERICULTURAL AN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUBOUCHI KOZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN AS REPRESENTED BY DIRECTOR GENERAL OF NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF SERICULTURAL AND ENTOMOLOGICAL SCIENCE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE, FORESTRY AND FISHERIES</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBOUCHI, KOZO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUBOUCHI KOZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUBOUCHI, KOZO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for industrially producing, through the physical pulverization of silk fibers, a crystalline silk fibroin powder having an average particle diameter smaller than 3  mu m which is usable in various applications. A silk material such as cocoon fiber, silk, or raw silk is contacted with an aqueous alkali solution at a temperature of 100 to 150  DEG C and a pressure of 1 to 5 atm to reduce the tensile strength of the silk material to about 0.02 g/d or lower, subsequently subjecting the silk material to alkali removal and drying, and then pulverizing the dried silk material to an average particle diameter smaller than 3  mu m. Thus, a crystalline silk fibroin powder having an average particle diameter smaller than 3  mu m is produced.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un procédé qui permet de produire de manière industrielle, par pulvérisation physique de fibres de soie, une poudre de fibroïne de soie cristalline dont le diamètre moyen des particules est inférieur à 3  mu m et qui peut être utilisée dans diverses applications. Un matériau à base de soie, telle que de la fibre de cocon, de la soie ou de la soie brute, est mis en contact avec une solution aqueuse d'alcali à une température de 100 à 150 DEG  C et à une pression de 1 à 5 atm, ceci de manière à réduire la résistance à la traction dudit matériau à environ 0,02 g/d ou moins. On élimine ensuite l'alcali du matériau à base de soie, on sèche ce dernier et, une fois séché, on le pulvérise en particules d'un diamètre moyen de moins de 3  mu m. On obtient ainsi une poudre de fibroïne de soie cristalline dont le diamètre moyen des particules est inférieur à 3  mu m.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>